WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
A car passes a roadside sign. You see it for a moment, then it's gone.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Later, another witness describes the sign. But their description is wrong.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
When you're asked what you saw, that later description can change your answer.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
This is the misinformation effect, demonstrated in classic experiments and revisited in a modern replication.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
The mechanism is still debated. A wrong answer is not proof that the original memory was erased.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Keep the first account. Trace the later questions. Then check the source. Final Vestige Studios.
